IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- THE DEALERS REGULATIONS 2003 AS MADE (S 185/2003) AND THEIR TWO AMENDMENTS OF 2004 (S 48/2004, S 593/2004), deposited 2026-11-04 from the second follow-up list (Part 3) under
-- subjects/sg/telecommunications-dealers-regulations-2003/registers/source-bundle/ (TA1999-RG6-S185-2003, TA1999-RG6-S48-2004, TA1999-RG6-S593-2004).
-- S 185/2003: first published 2 April 2003 at 5:00 pm, in operation 2 April 2003 (reg 1); made under s 74 of the Act (s 97 today).  Reg 26: "The Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 7) are revoked."
-- THAT FIXES THE END OF Rg 7 (1999 Ed.): its last day is 1 April 2003 (sgta-i-rg7-1999.l4), which until Part 3 was an assumption.
-- S 48/2004: first published 3 February 2004, in operation 3 February 2004; regs 9 and 10(1): "$400" replaced by "$250".
-- S 593/2004: first published 27 September 2004, in operation 1 October 2004; Second Schedule paragraph 5 replaced.
-- The 2004 Revised Edition (TA1999-RG6.txt, history line "[G.N. Nos. S 185/2003; S 48/2004; S 593/2004]", the file dated 31.12.2004) prints the Regulations as made and as amended by the two; its own start day (1 January 2005) is assumed (NOTES.md Fork B).
-- WHAT THIS MODULE ENCODES.  (1) A table of how each regulation of S 185/2003 compares, word for word, with the 2004 Revised Edition deposited as TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004.txt (by script, after setting aside case, punctuation other than the parentheses of
-- paragraph labels, hyphenation, running heads and page furniture; 31 blocks: 26 regulations and 5 Schedules; in 25 the words are the same and in 6 they differ, and for each of the 6 the difference is stated; the comparison text is TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004.txt, and the tail of the block for reg 25 (the heading of reg 26) and of the Fifth Schedule (the signature block against the Revised Edition's history line) are set aside).  Where the words are the same the
-- encoded rule of the Revised Edition is the as-made rule; where they differ the rule is NOT carried back.  (2) The effect of S 48/2004 and S 593/2004 as functions of both days.
-- The seat does not consult this module.

