-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:68 | The Schedules
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:71 | In exercise of the powers conferred by section 74 of the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:72 | Telecommunications Act, the Info-communications Development
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:73 | Authority of Singapore, with the approval of Mr David Lim Tik En,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:74 | Senior Minister of State, charged with the responsibility of the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:75 | Minister for Information, Communications and the Arts, hereby
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:76 | makes the following Regulations:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:79 | PART I
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:80 | PRELIMINARY
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:82 | Citation and commencement
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:83 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:84 | (Dealers) Regulations 2003 and shall come into operation on 2nd
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:85 | April 2003.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:87 | Definitions
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:88 | 2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:89 | ‘‘authorised officer’’ means any person authorised by the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:90 | Authority to act on its behalf;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:91 | ‘‘dealer’’ means a person who manufactures, imports for sale, lets
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:92 | for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale any equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:93 | which is capable of being used for the purpose of telecom-
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:94 | munication, and includes an employee of the dealer;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:95 | ‘‘Dealer’s Class Licence’’ means a licence referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:96 | regulation 3;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:97 | ‘‘Dealer’s Individual Licence’’ means a licence referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:98 | regulation 4;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:99 | ‘‘identity card’’ means an identity card issued under the National
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:100 | Registration Act (Cap. 201);
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:101 | ‘‘licence’’ means a Dealer’s Class Licence or a Dealer’s Individual
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:102 | Licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:103 | ‘‘licensee’’ means a person to whom a licence is granted, and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:104 | includes an employee of the licensee;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:105 | ‘‘registered equipment’’ means any telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:106 | registered for sale under regulation 21 (1);
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:107 | ‘‘sale’’ includes every transaction of or in the nature of barter
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:108 | or exchange, every transaction of hire or hire-purchase and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:109 | every transaction by which any goods are pawned or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:110 | hypothecated or as the result of which the ownership of or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:111 | an interest in goods is or may be transferred or created;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:114 | ‘‘telecommunication equipment’’ means any appliance,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:115 | apparatus or accessory used or intended to be used for
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:116 | telecommunications;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:117 | ‘‘type-approved equipment’’ means any telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:118 | equipment approved for sale under regulation 20 (1).
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:120 | PART II
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:121 | LICENSING OF DEALERS
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:123 | Dealer’s Class Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:124 | 3.—(1) Subject to regulation 7, a dealer who manufactures,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:125 | imports, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale any type-
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:126 | approved equipment, registered equipment or telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:127 | equipment set out in the First Schedule shall be deemed to have been
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:128 | granted a Dealer’s Class Licence under section 5 of the Act for that
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:129 | purpose.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:130 | (2) The holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall, in addition to
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:131 | any requirement imposed under these Regulations, comply with the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:132 | conditions of that licence set out in the Second Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:133 | (3) The Authority may impose any condition in addition to those
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:134 | referred to in paragraph (2) and may vary or waive all or any of such
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:135 | conditions.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:136 | (4) The holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall, at his own
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:137 | expense, comply with the varied or additional conditions referred to
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:138 | in paragraph (3).
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:139 | (5) The holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall register with the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:140 | Authority in such form as the Authority may determine each of the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:141 | premises under his control or occupation where he manufactures,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:142 | imports, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale any type-
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:143 | approved equipment, registered equipment or telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:144 | equipment set out in the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:145 | (6) The Authority shall acknowledge the registration under
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:146 | paragraph (5) to the licensee and the acknowledgment shall be in
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:147 | such form as the Authority may determine.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:148 | (7) For the purposes of paragraph (5), the holder of a Dealer’s Class
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:149 | Licence shall submit in writing to the Authority such information as
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:152 | the Authority may require relating to his particulars and the description
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:153 | and scope of his dealings in telecommunication equipment.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:154 | (8) The holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall furnish the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:155 | Authority with such specifications and information as the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:156 | may require on the types of telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:157 | manufactured, sold or to be manufactured or sold by him.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:158 | (9) The holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall notify the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:159 | Authority of any change in any particular furnished to the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:160 | under this regulation within 14 days of such change.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:161 | (10) No person shall furnish any false, misleading or inaccurate
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:162 | information to the Authority under this regulation.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:163 | (11) Where the holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence ceases to
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:164 | manufacture, import, let for hire, sell, or offer or possess for sale type-
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:165 | approved equipment, registered equipment or telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:166 | equipment set out in the First Schedule, the holder shall inform the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:167 | Authority of such cessation as soon as practicable.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:169 | Dealer’s Individual Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:170 | 4.—(1) A dealer who wishes to manufacture, import, let for hire,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:171 | sell, or offer or possess for sale any telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:172 | that is not —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:173 | (a) type-approved equipment;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:174 | (b) registered equipment; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:175 | (c) telecommunication equipment set out in the First Schedule,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:176 | shall obtain a Dealer’s Individual Licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:177 | (2) Every application for a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:178 | made in such form and manner as the Authority may, from time to
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:179 | time, determine and shall be supported by such information as the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:180 | Authority may require.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:181 | (3) No person shall furnish any false, misleading or inaccurate
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:182 | information for the purpose of obtaining a Dealer’s Individual
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:183 | Licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:184 | (4) The Authority shall notify the applicant as to whether his
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:185 | application is successful and the notification shall be in such form as
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:186 | the Authority may determine.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:189 | (5) Upon notification that his application is successful, the applicant
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:190 | shall pay to the Authority the fee referred to in regulation 10 (1) (a)
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:191 | and the Authority shall, subject to regulation 7, grant a Dealer’s
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:192 | Individual Licence under section 5 of the Act to the applicant upon
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:193 | receipt of such payment.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:194 | (6) When granting a Dealer’s Individual Licence, the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:195 | shall specify the types of telecommunication equipment which the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:196 | holder may manufacture, import, let for hire, sell, or offer or possess
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:197 | for sale.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:198 | (7) It shall be a condition of a Dealer’s Individual Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:199 | that the holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence may only sell
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:200 | telecommunication equipment that is not type-approved equipment,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:201 | registered equipment or telecommunication equipment set out in the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:202 | First Schedule —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:203 | (a) to another holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:204 | (b) to a person, other than the holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:205 | for re-export and not for use in Singapore.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:206 | (8) A dealer shall obtain a Dealer’s Individual Licence for each of
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:207 | the premises under his control or occupation where he manufactures,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:208 | imports, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:209 | telecommunication equipment referred to in paragraph (1).
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:210 | (9) The holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall notify the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:211 | Authority of any change in his personal particulars specified in that
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:212 | licence within 14 days of such change.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:213 | (10) A Dealer’s Individual Licence shall be valid for such period
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:214 | as the Authority may determine unless revoked or suspended in
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:215 | accordance with the provisions of the Act and shall be subject to such
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:216 | conditions as the Authority thinks fit.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:217 | (11) The Authority may add to, vary or waive all or any of, the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:218 | conditions referred to in paragraph (10) and the holder of a Dealer’s
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:219 | Individual Licence shall, at his own expense, comply with the varied
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:220 | or additional conditions.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:222 | When holder of Dealer’s Individual Licence is holder of Dealer’s
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:223 | Class Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:224 | 5.—(1) The holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence who
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:225 | manufactures, imports, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:226 | for sale any type-approved equipment, registered equipment or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:229 | telecommunication equipment set out in the First Schedule at
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:230 | premises other than those in respect of which he has obtained a
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:231 | Dealer’s Individual Licence shall be deemed to have been granted
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:232 | a Dealer’s Class Licence in respect of those other premises.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:233 | (2) The holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence who manufactures,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:234 | imports, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale any type-
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:235 | approved equipment, registered equipment or telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:236 | equipment set out in the First Schedule at the premises in respect of
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:237 | which he has obtained a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall not be
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:238 | deemed to be a holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence for such purpose
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:239 | in respect of those premises.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:241 | Operation for demonstration purpose
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:242 | 6.—(1) No person shall operate any telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:243 | for demonstration purposes unless he has obtained the prior approval
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:244 | of the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:245 | (2) It shall be a condition of every licence that a licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:246 | shall not, except with the prior approval of the Authority, operate
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:247 | any telecommunication equipment for demonstration purposes.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:249 | Restriction on grant of licence
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:250 | 7. No person shall be granted a Dealer’s Individual Licence or be
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:251 | deemed to have been granted a Dealer’s Class Licence unless that
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:252 | person is —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:253 | (a) a citizen of Singapore;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:254 | (b) a company incorporated under the Companies Act (Cap. 50);
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:255 | (c) a person who carries on a business registered under the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:256 | Business Registration Act (Cap. 32); or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:257 | (d) such other person as the Authority may, in its discretion,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:258 | consider appropriate to hold such licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:260 | Replacement of Dealer’s Individual Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:261 | 8. If the Authority is satisfied that any Dealer’s Individual Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:262 | issued by it has been lost, destroyed or defaced, the Authority may,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:263 | upon payment of a fee of $5 by the person whose Dealer’s Individual
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:264 | Licence is lost, destroyed or defaced, issue a replacement licence to
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:265 | such person.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:268 | Renewal of Dealer’s Individual Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:269 | 9. Every application for the renewal of a Dealer’s Individual
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:270 | Licence shall be in such form and manner as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:271 | require and accompanied by a renewal fee of $400.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:273 | Fees
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:274 | 10.—(1) The fee payable for a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:275 | as follows:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:276 | (a) $400 for the first year of that licence; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:277 | (b) $400 for every subsequent year for the duration of that
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:278 | licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:279 | (2) The fee payable for a Dealer’s Class Licence shall be as follows:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:280 | (a) $50 for the first 5 years from the date of the Authority’s
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:281 | acknowledgment under regulation 3 (6); and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:282 | (b) $50 for every subsequent period of 5 years for the duration
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:283 | of that licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:284 | (3) Payment of fees in respect of a Dealer’s Individual Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:285 | shall be made —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:286 | (a) in respect of a fee referred to in paragraph (1) (a), within
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:287 | 90 days of the notification under regulation 4 (4) that the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:288 | application for a Dealer’s Individual Licence is successful;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:289 | and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:290 | (b) in respect of a fee referred to in paragraph (1) (b), on or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:291 | before each anniversary of the date of issue of the Dealer’s
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:292 | Individual Licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:293 | (4) Payment of fees in respect of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:294 | made —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:295 | (a) in respect of a fee referred to in paragraph (2) (a), within
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:296 | 90 days of the date of the registration under regulation 3 (5);
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:297 | and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:298 | (b) in respect of a fee referred to in paragraph (2) (b), on or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:299 | before the anniversary of the date of the Authority’s
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:300 | acknowledgment under regulation 3 (6) at the end of each
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:301 | period of 5 years.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:302 | (5) If any fee remains unpaid after the date by which such fee
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:303 | should have been paid as referred to in paragraph (3) (b) or (4) (b),
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:304 | the following late payment fee shall be charged:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:307 | (a) where the fee is paid after 7 days but before 15 days
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:308 | following the date by which such fee should have been paid,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:309 | $10;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:310 | (b) where the fee is paid after 14 days but before 31 days
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:311 | following the date by which such fee should have been paid,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:312 | $20; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:313 | (c) where the fee is paid after 30 days following the date by
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:314 | which such fee should have been paid, $50.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:315 | (6) It shall be a condition of a licence that the fee referred to
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:316 | in paragraph (1) (b) or (2), as the case may be, shall be paid in
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:317 | accordance with this regulation.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:319 | PART III
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:320 | CONDUCT OF DEALERS
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:322 | Prohibited equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:323 | 11. It shall be a condition of a licence that the licensee shall not
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:324 | manufacture, import, let for hire, sell, or offer or possess for sale any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:325 | telecommunication equipment set out in the Third Schedule except
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:326 | where approved by the Authority and in accordance with such terms
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:327 | and conditions as the Authority may impose.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:329 | Equipment to be used for lawful purpose, safe manner, etc.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:330 | 12. A licensee shall ensure that any telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:331 | in his possession is not used for any unlawful purpose and shall
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:332 | operate it in a manner which is safe and which does not impair or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:333 | interfere with the efficient and convenient working or maintenance
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:334 | of any other telecommunication system or service authorised by the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:335 | Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:337 | Secrecy
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:338 | 13.—(1) Except as otherwise provided in these Regulations or by
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:339 | the terms and conditions of a licence, every dealer having access to
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:340 | any telecommunication —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:341 | (a) shall hold strictly secret all such telecommunication, other
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:342 | than a telecommunication transmitted or sent for general
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:343 | information;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:346 | (b) shall not, directly or indirectly, disclose the contents of the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:347 | telecommunication except —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:348 | (i) to a person entitled to become acquainted with the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:349 | telecommunication; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:350 | (ii) to an authorised officer,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:351 | or except where the disclosure is otherwise authorised or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:352 | required by law; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:353 | (c) shall not make any use of such telecommunication.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:354 | (2) No dealer having access to any telecommunication shall print
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:355 | or publish or cause to be printed or published in any newspaper,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:356 | pamphlet, book or other document, that telecommunication, whether
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:357 | such telecommunication is for private or general reception.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:359 | Restrictions on transmission
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:360 | 14.—(1) No dealer shall transmit or permit the transmission of
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:361 | superfluous signals.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:362 | (2) No person shall test any transmission, or allow or conduct
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:363 | any trial or practical transmission, except in such circumstances
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:364 | as to preclude the possibility of interference with any other
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:365 | telecommunication.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:366 | (3) No person shall conduct any test transmission other than on
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:367 | dummy load without the prior approval of the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:368 | (4) No dealer shall transmit or permit the transmission of —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:369 | (a) any message containing indecent, obscene or offensive
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:370 | language;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:371 | (b) any message for an illegal purpose;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:372 | (c) any message which interferes with the operation of any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:373 | type-approved equipment, registered equipment or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:374 | telecommunication equipment set out in the First Schedule;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:375 | or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:376 | (d) any message which to his knowledge is false or misleading
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:377 | and likely to prejudice the efficiency of any emergency
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:378 | service or endanger the safety of any person, place, premises,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:379 | vessel, aircraft or vehicle.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:382 | PART IV
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:383 | INSPECTION
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:385 | Inspection of Dealer’s Individual Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:386 | 15.—(1) The holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall permit
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:387 | an authorised officer or a police officer not below the rank of
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:388 | sergeant, upon production of proof of identity, to inspect his licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:389 | (2) Where his licence is not immediately available, the holder of a
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:390 | Dealer’s Individual Licence shall produce his licence at the office of
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:391 | the Authority or a police station named by the police officer within
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:392 | a reasonable period.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:394 | Inspection of equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:395 | 16.—(1) The Authority may appoint authorised officers as
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:396 | inspection officers for the inspection and examination of any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:397 | equipment approved under these Regulations, any premises owned
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:398 | or occupied by a dealer where he manufactures, imports, lets for
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:399 | hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale any telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:400 | equipment, and any telecommunication equipment found therein.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:401 | (2) For the purpose of ensuring that the Act, these Regulations
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:402 | and any condition of a licence are complied with, an inspection officer
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:403 | shall be entitled, at any time and upon production of proof of identity,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:404 | to enter any land, building, vessel, aircraft or vehicle where any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:405 | telecommunication equipment is kept or stored and to inspect,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:406 | examine or test such equipment.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:408 | Duty to give access
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:409 | 17. No person shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:410 | (a) refuse entry to an authorised officer to any land, building,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:411 | vessel, aircraft or vehicle to inspect, examine or test any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:412 | telecommunication equipment contained or stored therein;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:413 | or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:414 | (b) in any way obstruct or hinder an authorised officer in the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:415 | execution of a duty imposed or power conferred upon that
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:416 | officer by the Act, these Regulations or any other written
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:417 | law.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:420 | PART V
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:421 | IMPORT, MANUFACTURE AND
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:422 | SALE OF TELECOMMUNICATION EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:424 | Restrictions on importation of telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:425 | 18.—(1) No person shall import any telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:426 | without the prior approval of the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:427 | (2) A person applying for approval under paragraph (1) shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:428 | (a) furnish such particulars as may be required by the Authority;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:429 | and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:430 | (b) obtain a permit under the Regulation of Imports and Exports
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:431 | Regulations (Cap. 272A, Rg 1) for the equipment before such
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:432 | equipment is imported.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:433 | (3) No person shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:434 | (a) furnish any false or misleading information to the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:435 | for the purpose of obtaining the approval of the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:436 | under paragraph (1); or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:437 | (b) falsify or fabricate any decision that the Authority may make
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:438 | upon the application for approval under paragraph (1).
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:439 | (4) Where any person contravenes paragraph (3), any approval
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:440 | issued to that person under this regulation shall be null and void.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:442 | Power of Authority to order production of equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:443 | 19. The Authority may direct a person who imports any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:444 | telecommunication equipment to produce it for testing or inspection
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:445 | by the Authority and that person shall comply with such direction at
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:446 | his own expense.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:448 | Application for type-approval
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:449 | 20.—(1) Subject to paragraph (2) and regulation 4 (7), it shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:450 | a condition of a licence that the licensee shall not sell —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:451 | (a) any type of telecommunication equipment to be used for
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:452 | connection to any telecommunication system or equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:453 | belonging to a telecommunication system licensee; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:454 | (b) any type of radio-communication equipment to be used in
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:455 | Singapore,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:458 | unless the type of equipment has been approved by the Authority to
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:459 | be sold.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:460 | (2) No approval for sale under paragraph (1) is required in respect
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:461 | of any registered equipment or any telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:462 | set out in the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:463 | (3) An application for type-approval of any equipment referred to
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:464 | in paragraph (1) shall be made to the Authority in such manner as
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:465 | the Authority may determine.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:466 | (4) No dealer shall furnish any false or misleading information
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:467 | to the Authority for the purpose of obtaining any approval under
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:468 | paragraph (1).
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:469 | (5) Where any dealer contravenes paragraph (4), any approval
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:470 | issued to that dealer under this regulation shall be null and void.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:471 | (6) The fee for an application for approval under paragraph (1)
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:472 | is specified in the Fourth Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:474 | Application for registration of equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:475 | 21.—(1) Upon an application in such form as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:476 | determine, the Authority may register for sale any telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:477 | equipment which has been certified or tested by such body as the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:478 | Authority may determine.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:479 | (2) The registration under paragraph (1) shall be valid for 5 years
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:480 | and upon an application for renewal in such form as the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:481 | may determine, may be renewed for periods not exceeding 5 years at
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:482 | a time.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:483 | (3) The fee payable for registration shall be $100 for the first
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:484 | 5 years and $50 for every renewed period of 5 years or less.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:486 | PART VI
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:487 | TESTING
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:489 | Testing of telecommunication equipment for personal use
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:490 | 22.—(1) The Authority may, at the request of any person intending
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:491 | to use any telecommunication equipment or type of telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:492 | equipment for personal purpose, test that equipment to verify that the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:493 | equipment is designed, constructed, installed, established, maintained
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:496 | or operated in accordance with such technical specifications as the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:497 | Authority may determine.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:498 | (2) The Authority may, in its discretion, impose the fees specified
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:499 | in the Fifth Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:500 | (3) Paragraph (1) shall not apply to any radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:501 | equipment that is not type-approved equipment.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:503 | PART VII
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:504 | MISCELLANEOUS
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:506 | Power to order disposal of equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:507 | 23. Where any person —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:508 | (a) imports any telecommunication equipment without the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:509 | approval of the Authority; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:510 | (b) manufactures, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:511 | sale any telecommunication equipment which does not meet
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:512 | the standards or specifications published by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:513 | from time to time,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:514 | the Authority may direct that person to dispose of the equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:515 | in any manner which the Authority thinks fit and that person shall
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:516 | comply with such direction at his own expense.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:518 | Offence
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:519 | 24. Any person who contravenes regulation 3 (5), (7), (8), (9) or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:520 | (10), 4 (3), (8) or (9), 6 (1), 12, 13, 14, 15, 17, 18 (1), (2) or (3), 19,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:521 | 20 (4) or 23 shall be guilty of an offence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:523 | Waiver and exemption
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:524 | 25.—(1) The Minister, or the Authority with the approval of the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:525 | Minister, may —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:526 | (a) waive any or all fees payable under these Regulations; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:527 | (b) exempt any person from any or all provisions of these
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:528 | Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:529 | (2) A waiver or an exemption granted under paragraph (1) may
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:530 | be notified in writing to the person concerned, and need not be
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:531 | published in the Gazette.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:534 | Revocation
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:535 | 26. The Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 7) are
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:536 | revoked.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:538 | FIRST SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:539 | Regulations 3 (1), (5) and (11),
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:540 | 4 (1) and (7), 5, 14 (4) and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:541 | 20 (2) and paragraphs 1
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:542 | and 2 of Second Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:544 | TELECOMMUNICATION EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:545 | NOT REQUIRING APPROVAL
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:547 | 1. Telephone (Standard/Multi-Feature/Image/Data/Switching)
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:549 | 2. Telephone Line Interface
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:551 | 3. Telephone Ancillary
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:553 | 4. Autodialler
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:555 | 5. Auto Answering/Recording Set
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:557 | 6. Caller Identification Equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:559 | 7. Security Alarm System
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:561 | 8. Facsimile Transceiver
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:563 | 9. Voice Band Modem
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:565 | 10. EFTPOS/CCAT
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:567 | 11. Telex Equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:569 | 12. Digital Leased Circuit Equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:571 | 13. Other equipment as determined by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:574 | SECOND SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:575 | Regulation 3 (2)
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:577 | CONDITIONS OF DEALER’S CLASS LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:579 | 1. The holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence (referred to in this Schedule as the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:580 | Class Licensee) shall manufacture, import, let for hire, sell, or offer or possess for
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:581 | sale only —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:582 | (a) telecommunication equipment approved for sale under regulation 20 (1);
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:583 | (b) telecommunication equipment registered for sale under regulation
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:584 | 21 (1); or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:585 | (c) telecommunication equipment set out in the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:587 | 2. A Class Licensee who wishes to sell any registered equipment or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:588 | telecommunication equipment set out in the First Schedule shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:589 | (a) before selling such telecommunication equipment, ensure that it meets
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:590 | the standards and specifications for the sale of such telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:591 | equipment published by the Authority in the manner it thinks fit;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:592 | (b) ensure that it works correctly with the relevant telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:593 | system or equipment of the telecommunication system licensee to which
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:594 | it is connected; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:595 | (c) cease to sell the telecommunication equipment if so directed by the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:596 | Authority and dispose of the telecommunication equipment at his own
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:597 | expense in the manner directed by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:599 | 3. A Class Licensee shall, if required by the Authority, produce any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:600 | telecommunication equipment for testing or inspection by the Authority and all
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:601 | expenses incurred in connection with the testing or inspection shall be borne by the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:602 | Class Licensee.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:604 | 4. A Class Licensee shall not have in his possession for sale any device or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:605 | equipment which is capable of monitoring or intercepting the transmission of a
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:606 | radio-communication network.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:608 | 5. A Class Licensee shall not have in his possession for sale, or use any device
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:609 | or equipment which can be used to alter, delete or remove the ESN, MIN or PIN
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:610 | number of any registered telecommunication equipment or to insert or duplicate
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:611 | the ESN, MIN or PIN number of any registered telecommunication equipment in
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:612 | any unregistered telecommunication equipment.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:614 | 6.—(1) A Class Licensee who imports any telecommunication equipment into
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:615 | Singapore for the purpose of re-export —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:616 | (a) shall, unless the Authority otherwise directs, immediately move the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:617 | telecommunication equipment into a free trade zone under the Free
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:618 | Trade Zones Act (Cap. 114) and keep it there pending re-export;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:619 | (b) shall not sell it to any person for use in Singapore; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:622 | SECOND SCHEDULE — continued
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:624 | (c) shall re-export the telecommunication equipment and furnish
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:625 | satisfactory evidence of the re-export to the Authority within such time
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:626 | as may be stipulated by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:627 | (2) A Class Licensee shall, if required by the Authority, give a written
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:628 | undertaking that the telecommunication equipment declared to be for export
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:629 | purposes will not be sold, or offered or possessed for sale in Singapore.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:631 | 7. A Class Licensee shall not manufacture, let for hire, sell, or offer or possess
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:632 | for sale any telecommunication equipment set out in the Third Schedule or any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:633 | telecommunication equipment which does not meet the standards or specifications
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:634 | published by the Authority from time to time.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:636 | 8. A Class Licensee shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:637 | (a) affix or ensure that there is affixed, on all type-approved equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:638 | intended for use in Singapore, labels stating or indicating that the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:639 | telecommunication equipment is type-approved before such
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:640 | telecommunication equipment is displayed or offered for sale;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:641 | (b) affix or ensure that there is affixed such other labels as the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:642 | considers necessary on any telecommunication equipment before such
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:643 | telecommunication equipment is displayed or offered for sale;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:644 | (c) ensure that every advertisement, pamphlet or brochure relating to any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:645 | telecommunication equipment which he sells or offers for sale contains
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:646 | such information as the Authority may specify;
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:647 | (d) refrain from affixing, on any telecommunication equipment which is not
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:648 | type-approved equipment, any label stating or indicating that the
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:649 | telecommunication equipment is type-approved; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:650 | (e) comply with such other labelling requirements as may be published by
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:651 | the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:653 | 9. A Class Licensee shall inform every purchaser or hirer to whom he sells or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:654 | lets for hire any telecommunication equipment of the need to obtain a licence from
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:655 | the Authority under the Act and these Regulations for the possession, operation,
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:656 | installation or use of that telecommunication equipment.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:658 | 10. Except with the Authority’s prior written consent, a Class Licensee shall
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:659 | not assign, transfer, sublet or otherwise dispose of any benefit of his Dealer’s Class
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:660 | Licence, or permit any person to participate in any benefit or authority granted by
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:661 | his licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:663 | 11. In addition to the conditions of the Dealer’s Class Licence, a Class
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:664 | Licensee shall comply with the provisions of the Act, these Regulations and any
-- src:TA1999-RG6-S185-2003:665 | code of practice issued under the Act.
